    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change lives entirely in one small function class \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 so structural impact is minimal (one file, one changed method with low surrounding complexity).\n\n**customerCode format** \u2014 now `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n- `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- `LAST3` \u2014 first three of the lastName\n- `NNNN` \u2014 per-city 4-digit sequence (owners already in that city, +1), computed by filtering `findAll()` on matching city\n\n**Derived values** \u2014 the membership number in `OwnerMapper` is built as `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), \u2026)`, reading `customerCode` at runtime, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format with no edit needed. That's the only derived value in the codebase.\n\nI kept the method simple by extracting two tiny private helpers (`prefix3`, `countInCity`) rather than growing the single `service` method or spreading logic across other classes.",
